From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:49:56 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: remove the peripheral-to-peripheral relay

The buffer manager's probe armed a relay that copies frames out of the
first switch macro's receive descriptor ring straight into the second
macro's transmit controller, without the processor seeing them. It
belongs to a topology in which the processor is not in the forwarding
path at all.

The network device that drives this datapath now terminates that receive
ring itself, and stops the relay channel before it repoints the ring,
precisely because the two cannot both consume it. So the relay is armed
at probe and switched off again a moment later, having never carried a
frame: no caller ever reaches the function that starts it, and the only
other reference to those channels is the stop.

Remove the arming, the start that nothing calls, and the two flags that
sequenced them. The stop stays where it is: it costs one register write
and it is the only thing standing between a ring this driver has taken
over and a relay a previous boot may have left running.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

